-- title:
--   Lemma 6.3 — discounted Markov chains as absorbing reachability
-- statement:
--   Consider a Markov chain $C=(S,\delta)$ with a reward function $r:S\to[0,1]$ and a discount factor $\lambda\in[0,1)$. Let $C^{\mathrm{abs}}$ be the chain with states $S\cup\{\top,\bot\}$, where $\top$ and $\bot$ are absorbing and, for all $s,s'\in S$,
--   $$\delta^{\mathrm{abs}}(s)(s')=\lambda\delta(s)(s'),\qquad\delta^{\mathrm{abs}}(s)(\top)=(1-\lambda)r(s),\qquad\delta^{\mathrm{abs}}(s)(\bot)=(1-\lambda)(1-r(s)).$$
--   Then $C^{\mathrm{abs}}$ is absorbing (from every state an absorbing state is reached with probability one), and for every $s\in S$,
--   $$\mathrm{val}^C_\lambda(s)=\mathrm{val}^{C^{\mathrm{abs}}}_\top(s).$$
--
--   This lets relative perturbation bounds for reachability, which do not depend on $\lambda$, control discounted values.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
--   - encoding: a Markov chain C = (S, δ) → a game with both action sets Fin 1 (CSG n 1 1); its reachability value is the probability of reaching the target; reason: the source defines an MC as the special CSG where both players have one action
--   - encoding: S ∪ {⊤, ⊥} → Fin (n + 2) with s ↦ Fin.castAdd 2 s, ⊤ = Fin.natAdd n 0, ⊥ = Fin.natAdd n 1; reason: relabelling
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Lemma 6.3, printed p. 20 (PDF p. 22)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Lemma 6.3 (Discounted-sum as reachability).** For a Markov chain `C = (S, δ)` with reward
`r : S → [0,1]` and discount factor `λ ∈ [0,1)`, the chain `C^abs` on `S ∪ {⊤, ⊥}` is absorbing,
and `val^C_λ(s) = val^{C^abs}_⊤(s)` for every `s ∈ S`. -/
theorem lemma_6_3 {n : ℕ} (C : CSG n 1 1) (r : Fin n → ℝ) (hr : ∀ s, 0 ≤ r s ∧ r s ≤ 1)
    (lam : ℝ) (hlam : 0 ≤ lam ∧ lam < 1) :
    IsAbsorbingMC (absChain C r hr lam hlam) ∧
    ∀ s : Fin n, discValue C (mcReward r) lam s =
      reachValue (absChain C r hr lam hlam) {absTop n} (Fin.castAdd 2 s) := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
